## DESCRIPTION
## Functions: Input and Output
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Algebra)
## DBchapter(Exponential and logarithmic expressions and functions)
## DBsection(Applications and models - general)
## Date(01/01/10)
## Institution(Fort Lewis College)
## Author(Paul Pearson)
## Level(4)
## TitleText1('Functions Modeling Change')
## AuthorText1('Connally')
## EditionText1('3')
## Section1('3.2')
## Problem1('38')
## KEYWORDS('exponential functions','annual growth rate','linear growth')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

@shuffle = random_subset(5, 0 .. 4);
@inv[@shuffle] = 0 .. 4;

$a      = random(10, 50, 5);
$b      = random(10, 50, 5);
$b0     = 1 - $b / 100;
$b1     = $b / 100;
$yr     = random(1940, 1970, 10);
$people = random(150,  400,  50);
$pop    = random(3000, 9000, 1000);
$pct    = random(4,    12);

@forms = (
    'f(x) = A(2)^{-x}',
    "f(x) = B($b0)^x",
    "f(x) = B($b1)^x",
    'f(x) = P_0 + r x',
    'f(x) = P_0(1 + r)^x'
);

@dd = map { DropDown([ 'A' .. 'E' ], $inv[$_]) } (0 .. 4);

BEGIN_PGML

Match each story with a formula.  Assume that the
constants [` P_0, r, b, A `] are all positive.

1. The percent of a lake's surface covered by algae, initially at [$a]%, was halved each year since the passage of anti-pollution laws. [_]{$dd[0]}

2. The amount of charge on a capacitor in an electric circuit decreases by [$b]% each second. [_]{$dd[1]}


3. Polluted water is passed through a series of filters.  Each filter removes all but [$b]% of the remaining impurities from the water. [_]{$dd[2]}

4. In [$yr], the population of a town was [$pop] people. Over the course of the next 50 years, the town  grew at a rate of [$people] people per year. [_]{$dd[3]}

5. In [$yr], the population of a town was [$pop] people. Over the course of the next 50 years, the town  grew at a rate of [$pct]% per decade. [_]{$dd[4]}

A. [`[$forms[$shuffle[0]]]`]
B. [`[$forms[$shuffle[1]]]`]
C. [`[$forms[$shuffle[2]]]`]
D. [`[$forms[$shuffle[3]]]`]
E. [`[$forms[$shuffle[4]]]`]

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
1. The [$a]% seems like a rate, but it isn't.  If it is halved every year, this is expondential with factor 0.5, however can also be done with a form of [` 2^{-1} `].  The answer is *[$dd[0]]****

2. If  the rate decreases [$b]% each second, then first, it is exponential and secondly, the rate is [$b0], so the answer is *[$dd[1]]****

3. In this case, the rate is [$b]% and is exponential, so the answer is *[$dd[2]]****

4. Since the town grows by a fixed number of people per year, this is linear and the form is that in *[$dd[3]]****.

5. Since the town grows by a percentage each year, then it is exponetial with a rate greater than 1 or [`1+r`], so the answer is *[$dd[4]]****
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
